body.proof_tex:
Write \(I_{a,s}=\mathbf 1\{G=a,S=s\}\), \(p_{a,s}(x)=P(G=a,S=s\mid X=x)\), \(\pi=E_P[p_{g,1}(X)]\), and \(\mu_{a,s}(x)=E_P[D\mid G=a,S=s,X=x]\). In this one-period target,
\[
q(x)=\mu_{g,1}(x)-\mu_{g,0}(x)-\mu_{c,1}(x)+\mu_{c,0}(x),
\qquad
\theta=\frac{E_P[p_{g,1}(X)q(X)]}{\pi}.
\tag{R1}
\]
Definition \(\ref{def:pairwise-score}\) therefore specializes to
\[
\begin{aligned}
\Psi_{k,c,P}
=\frac1\pi\bigg[&I_{g,1}\{q(X)-\theta+D-\mu_{g,1}(X)\}
-I_{g,0}\frac{p_{g,1}(X)}{p_{g,0}(X)}\{D-\mu_{g,0}(X)\}\\
&-I_{c,1}\frac{p_{g,1}(X)}{p_{c,1}(X)}\{D-\mu_{c,1}(X)\}
+I_{c,0}\frac{p_{g,1}(X)}{p_{c,0}(X)}\{D-\mu_{c,0}(X)\}\bigg].
\end{aligned}
\tag{R2}
\]
Overlap makes all displayed ratios well defined.

Lemma \(\ref{lem:causal-identification}\) identifies the source's \(\operatorname{ATT}(2,2)\), after the cohort relabeling, with \(\theta\) in (R1). Likewise, the displayed definition of \(\psi_{\mathrm{pd}}\) in the Akbari--Kiyavash--Ghassami specialization and iterated expectation give
\[
\psi_{\mathrm{pd}}
=\frac{E_P[p_{g,1}(X)q(X)]}{\pi}=\theta.
\tag{R3}
\]

For each comparison cell \((a,s)\), iterated expectation gives
\[
E_P\!\left[I_{a,s}\frac{p_{g,1}(X)}{p_{a,s}(X)}\right]
=E_P[p_{g,1}(X)]=\pi.
\tag{R4}
\]
After the relabeling \((2,\infty)\mapsto(g,c)\) and \(E\mapsto S\), the source weights in Ortiz--Villavicencio and Sant'Anna's Lemma A.2 are therefore \(I_{g,1}/\pi\) for the target cell and \(I_{a,s}p_{g,1}(X)/\{\pi p_{a,s}(X)\}\) for each comparison cell. Moreover,
\[
\tau(X)-\theta
=D-\mu_{g,0}(X)-\mu_{c,1}(X)+\mu_{c,0}(X)-\theta
=D-\mu_{g,1}(X)+q(X)-\theta.
\tag{R5}
\]
Substitution of (R4)--(R5) into that cited formula gives exactly the four terms in (R2).

For the formula in Akbari, Kiyavash, and Ghassami's Theorem 5, relabel \(G_A=1\) as \(G=g\), \(G_A=0\) as \(G=c\), and \(D_A=S\). Then \(G_AD_A=I_{g,1}\), \(\pi_{r,a,s}(X)=p_{g,1}(X)/p_{a,s}(X)\), and their source formula becomes
\[
\begin{aligned}
\eta_A
=\frac1\pi\sum_{a,s\in\{0,1\}}(-1)^{a+s+1}
\left\{I_{g,1}-I_{a,s}\frac{p_{g,1}(X)}{p_{a,s}(X)}\right\}
\{D-\mu_{a,s}(X)\}
-\frac{I_{g,1}}\pi\theta.
\end{aligned}
\tag{R6}
\]
The four signs for \((a,s)=(0,0),(0,1),(1,0),(1,1)\) are \((-1,1,1,-1)\). Their sum is zero, so the common \(I_{g,1}D\) terms in (R6) cancel, and
\[
-\sum_{a,s}(-1)^{a+s+1}\mu_{a,s}(X)
=\mu_{c,0}(X)-\mu_{c,1}(X)-\mu_{g,0}(X)+\mu_{g,1}(X)
=q(X).
\tag{R7}
\]
The cell-specific part has coefficients \(+1,-1,-1,+1\) on the comparison-ineligible, comparison-eligible, target-ineligible, and target-eligible residuals. Equations (R6)--(R7) thus reproduce (R2) term by term, including the denominator derivative \(-I_{g,1}\theta/\pi\).

Finally, a singleton clean set has no pair of distinct clean cohorts, so Definition \(\ref{def:ovs-normal-projection}\) gives a zero-dimensional \(Z_P^{\mathrm{OVS}}\) and \(p_{\mathrm{OVS},P}=0\). With one target and unit weight, \(\psi_P^0=\Psi_{k,c,P}\). Theorem \(\ref{thm:complete-normal-canonical-gradient}\) then yields \(\phi_{\mathrm{OVS},P}=\Psi_{k,c,P}\). Linearity gives the scalar-weight claim. Chen, Sant'Anna, and Xie study a staggered-DiD observation and restriction system without the eligibility coordinate \(S\); since no map between their tangent space and the present four-cell eligibility-gap tangent system has been proved here, no nesting claim follows from the algebra above.
